Feature: Specification.MD keeps one copy of the BL-607 paragraph, not 286

  One commit appended the same ~2,900-character paragraph 286 times through
  the tail of docs/reference/Specification.MD, taking the file from 503 KB to
  1.36 MB. 284 of those copies also carry a shell-mangled CLI example, so the
  two copies that are correct are the minority — a dedupe that keeps the most
  common copy keeps the broken one.

  The repair deletes 285 copies and nothing else. Markdown legitimately
  repeats code fences, horizontal rules and table separators; those must
  survive untouched.

  Background:
    Given a Specification.MD holding 286 copies of one paragraph
    And 284 of those copies carry a mangled CLI example
    And 2 of those copies carry the correct CLI example

  # BL-692 spec-dup-repair-01
  Scenario: exactly one copy survives
    When the duplicate-paragraph repair runs
    Then the document holds exactly 1 copy of that paragraph

  # BL-692 spec-dup-repair-02
  Scenario: the surviving copy is the correct one, not the common one
    When the duplicate-paragraph repair runs
    Then the surviving copy carries the correct CLI example
    And no mangled CLI example remains in the document

  # BL-692 spec-dup-repair-03
  Scenario: the surviving copy stays where it belongs in the narrative
    When the duplicate-paragraph repair runs
    Then the surviving copy sits between the BL-354 paragraph and the BL-283 paragraph

  # BL-692 spec-dup-repair-04
  Scenario Outline: markdown that is supposed to repeat is left alone
    Given the document repeats the structural line <line>
    When the duplicate-paragraph repair runs
    Then every occurrence of <line> survives

    Examples:
      | line              |
      | code fence        |
      | horizontal rule   |
      | table separator   |
      | diagram glyph     |

  # BL-692 spec-dup-repair-05
  Scenario: no real content is lost
    When the duplicate-paragraph repair runs
    Then every non-blank line other than the removed copies is byte-identical and in the same order

  # BL-692 spec-dup-repair-06
  Scenario: the blank lines the corruption doubled are collapsed
    When the duplicate-paragraph repair runs
    Then no run of two consecutive blank lines remains in the document

  # BL-692 spec-dup-repair-07
  Scenario: the repaired document is the measured size
    When the duplicate-paragraph repair runs
    Then the document is 2249 lines long

  # BL-692 spec-dup-repair-08
  Scenario: repairing an already-repaired document changes nothing
    When the duplicate-paragraph repair runs
    And the duplicate-paragraph repair runs again
    Then the document holds exactly 1 copy of that paragraph
    And the second run left the document unchanged
